Talia, I went through the model this afternoon. Three small things and one th=
at I think is structural.

Small: the instrument tab has two columns with the same header, the sensitivi=
ty tab is hard-coded in one cell that should reference the input block, and t=
he summary tab rounds before it aggregates rather than after. None of those c=
hange a conclusion but all three will be found by whoever checks this next.

The structural one is that the model reads two different sources for the same=
 input depending on which tab you are on. That is how a model becomes interna=
lly inconsistent without anybody making a mistake. It needs one input block a=
nd everything else pointing at it.

I do not think this is a rebuild. It is a morning of plumbing. But do the plu=
mbing before you add the scenario grid, not after.

Kip, worth reading this even though it is not your file. Every model you will=
 ever be handed has some version of the fourth problem.

